{
  "id": "events",
  "title": "Handling events",
  "summary": "`on:<event>` calls a service method or sets a service field when the event happens. You can use `$event` (the browser event object) and limited dotted paths (names joined by dots). A JavaScript or TypeScript method receives the browser event first and then the arguments from the view. A method in any other language receives only the arguments. A Python service also needs the `tac.python` runtime setting in `client/manifest.json`.",
